---
import PureRunLayout from '../../layouts/PureRunLayout.astro';
---

<PureRunLayout
  title="PureRun — A private running app for iPhone and Apple Watch"
  description="PureRun is a clean running app for iPhone and Apple Watch. Track live metrics and progress with HealthKit, without accounts, feeds, advertising, or PureRun servers."
  keywords="PureRun, running app, run tracker, Apple Watch, iPhone, HealthKit, private running app, workout mirroring"
  current="overview"
>
  <section class="relative isolate overflow-hidden bg-[#090b0d] text-white">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(circle_at_75%_25%,rgba(167,255,47,0.18),transparent_32%)]" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="relative mx-auto grid max-w-5xl items-center gap-16 px-6 py-24 sm:py-32 lg:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr] lg:px-8">
      <div>
        <p class="mb-5 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#a7ff2f]">iPhone + Apple Watch</p>
        <h1 class="max-w-3xl text-5xl font-black tracking-[-0.04em] sm:text-7xl">
          Run. See progress.<br />Keep it private.
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-2xl text-xl leading-8 text-gray-300">
          PureRun tracks the run and gets out of your way. No login, no feed, no ads, and no PureRun server—just clear live metrics and your running history in HealthKit.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-[#a7ff2f] px-7 py-4 text-base font-bold text-black">
            Coming to the App Store
          </span>
          <a href="/purerun/support" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-white/20 px-7 py-4 text-base font-bold text-white transition-colors hover:border-[#a7ff2f] hover:text-[#a7ff2f]">
            Get support
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-sm rounded-[2.5rem] border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.06] p-5 shadow-2xl shadow-[#a7ff2f]/10">
        <div class="rounded-[2rem] bg-black p-7 ring-1 ring-white/10">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-sm font-bold">
            <span class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-[#a7ff2f]"></span>RUNNING</span>
            <span class="text-gray-500">LIVE</span>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-10 text-center text-6xl font-black tracking-tight">32:18</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-center text-3xl font-bold text-[#a7ff2f]">5.24 km</p>
          <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 border-t border-white/10 pt-6">
            <div>
              <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-500">Heart</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xl font-bold">148 bpm</p>
            </div>
            <div class="text-right">
              <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-500">Pace</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xl font-bold">6:10 /km</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y border-lime-200 bg-lime-50 dark:border-lime-900 dark:bg-lime-950/40">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-5xl gap-8 px-6 py-9 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:px-8">
      {[
        ['No account', 'Open the app and run. There is nothing to create or remember.'],
        ['No PureRun server', 'Workout data stays with Apple Health on your devices.'],
        ['No distractions', 'No social feed, advertising, analytics, or third-party SDKs.'],
      ].map(([title, text]) => (
        <div>
          <p class="font-bold text-lime-950 dark:text-lime-100">{title}</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-lime-900/75 dark:text-lime-200/75">{text}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white py-24 dark:bg-gray-900 sm:py-32">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-lime-600 dark:text-[#a7ff2f]">One workout, two screens</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-gray-950 dark:text-white sm:text-5xl">The Watch records. The iPhone keeps you company.</h2>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          Start from either device. Apple Watch records the workout and PureRun mirrors its live state to your iPhone, giving you a larger companion display without creating a second workout.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
        {[
          ['Start simply', 'Begin an outdoor run from iPhone or Apple Watch, then pause, resume, or end it from either screen.'],
          ['See what matters', 'Follow elapsed time, distance, pace, heart rate, and active energy while you move.'],
          ['Review progress', 'See recent runs and your last seven days directly from workouts stored in HealthKit.'],
        ].map(([title, text], index) => (
          <article class="rounded-3xl border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-7 dark:border-gray-700 dark:bg-gray-800">
            <p class="text-sm font-black text-lime-600 dark:text-[#a7ff2f]">0{index + 1}</p>
            <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold text-gray-950 dark:text-white">{title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">{text}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-gray-100 py-24 dark:bg-gray-800 sm:py-32">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-5xl items-start gap-14 px-6 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:px-8">
      <div>
        <p class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-lime-600 dark:text-[#a7ff2f]">Private by construction</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-gray-950 dark:text-white">Your health information is not our business.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-7 text-lg leading-8 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
        <p>PureRun requests only the Health access needed to record runs, display live workout metrics, and show your history.</p>
        <p>It does not collect or transmit personal information or health data. There is no PureRun account, analytics service, advertising service, third-party SDK, or PureRun-operated server.</p>
        <a href="/purerun/privacy" class="inline-flex font-bold text-lime-700 hover:text-lime-600 dark:text-[#a7ff2f]">
          Read the privacy policy →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-[#a7ff2f] py-20 text-black">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 text-center lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-black tracking-tight">Nothing between you and the run.</h2>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-black/70">Built natively with SwiftUI and HealthKit for iPhone on iOS 17 or later and Apple Watch on watchOS 10 or later.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
    name: 'PureRun',
    applicationCategory: 'HealthApplication',
    operatingSystem: 'iOS 17 or later; watchOS 10 or later',
    description: 'A private running app for iPhone and Apple Watch with live HealthKit workout mirroring.',
    url: new URL('/purerun', Astro.site).toString(),
    author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Dale Hurley' },
  })} />
</PureRunLayout>
